   •  Show/hide the text lines for the notes below;
   •  Show/hide the Companion's Appearance box;
   •  Show/hide the Equipment section.

Here you can find the options for this Companion page:
   •  Create Familiar (as per the Find Familiar spell);
   •  Create Pact of the Chain familiar (as per the Pact of the Chain class ability);
   •  Create Mount (as per the Find Steed spell);
   •  Create Ranger's Companion;
   •  Apply one of the above to the current creature;
   •  Reset this entire page;
   •  Show/hide the Companion's Appearance box;
   •  Show/hide the Equipment section;
   •  Add another 'Companion' page;
   •  Remove this 'Companion' page.

If you just want to add a creature that has none of the special abilities granted by Find Familiar, Pact of the Chain, or Find Steed, just use the drop-down box next to "Race:".

With this button you can set the value of the maximum hit points field to one of the calculated values:
 • The total average HP;
 • The total HP when using fixed values;
 • The total maximum HP.

You can also set the field to automatically assume a calculated hit point value every time it changes.
